completed_at: "2026-08-26T21:14:30.897Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T22:32:16.249Z",claude,"Correcting this record's own close reason rather than editing it, because history here is append-only. The close reason says all six code fixes carry revert-verified tests. That is wrong, and the note on the same item already said so: two of the six were pure refactors - reusing parseJsonRecord, and removing a duplicated comment sentence - with identical behaviour and therefore no test that can fail on revert. The defensible count for round 6 is four of six revert-verified, with two refactors carrying no behavioural test by construction. Round 7 adds three more revert-verified fixes: the TypeScript type-annotation false positive, the episode repository refusal prefix, and the __proto__ search-space dimension. Claiming coverage that does not exist is worse than reporting less, because it is the number a later reader trusts."
  "2026-08-26T22:32:16.673Z",claude,"Round-7 code findings, all three valid and all three revert-verified. The unquoted assigned-secret alternative matched 'token: string' because string is exactly six characters, so assertNoCredentials refused ordinary TypeScript patches before rl episode record could hash them - a scan that blocks correct work is worse than the leak it prevents. It now excludes TypeScript type keywords rather than requiring an equals sign, because requiring one would stop refusing 'api_key: hunter22secret', which is the shape the scan exists to catch. parseEpisodeSpec refused a blank repository with the invalid_gate_environment_ prefix while every other field of the episode body used invalid_episode_, so a caller branching on the code blamed the wrong document. And parseSweepSpec assigned search-space dimensions with searchSpace[key] = values, which for the key __proto__ invokes the inherited setter instead of creating an own property: expandSearchSpace then saw no keys and returned an empty arm list, silently dropping a declared dimension while the sweep still looked like it ran."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T21:14:27.037Z",pi-agent,"All 8 round-6 findings resolved: 6 VALID code fixes (gate name trimming, unquoted secret scanning, resolved sweep id reporting, parseJsonRecord reuse, duplicated comment removal, dependency marker consolidation), 1 VALID pm data provenance fix (malformed test title apostrophe), 1 INVALID (stale open-status claim on already-closed task). Revert-proof verification: 4 of 6 code fixes have tests that FAIL on revert. The parseJsonRecord reuse and comment cleanup are pure refactors with no behavioral change. Gates: 237/237 tests, coverage 100/100/100/100 across 17 files, docstring 129 declarations, jscpd 0 clones, changelog check green."
